# DIT-OS userland C

Before editing matching files, read `.agents/skills/c-userland/SKILL.md` and follow
it. Also apply `AGENTS.md` (definition of done, handoff, hard rules) and the
mandatory `.agents/skills/security-audit/SKILL.md` for every code change.
Content lives in the skill; this file only points to it.

Never forget:
- Userland is freestanding flat binaries embedded in the kernel; no libc.a.
- Never include kernel headers; only syscalls via userland/include/syscall.h.
- Check the index before reading the element; check every syscall return.
